### S1 | type: add | dimension: member-family | symbol: described_physical_actions
- Needs: n1 (t1:s1), n4/n5 (t2:s2), n11 (t2:s4), n17/n18 (t2:s6), n22/n26 (t2:s8).
- Searches tried: search "describe requested placement spatial relation destination", "action description ordered procedure", "described movement destination direction route", "pick up description source behind vase"; widen "describe placing acquired keys on ottoman without execution", "turn left turn around go through living room to purple ottoman described instruction"; closest entries place/pick_up/walk/turn execute REQUEST work, RECORD falsely implies occurrence, activity lacks the needed roles, sequence only orders already constructed descriptions, obligation wraps an activity without supplying its roles.
- Shared category rules: Pure TERM constructors for described physical actions, usable as request/propose targets; not executable operations, assertions, recorded events or reference-acquisition mechanisms. TERM targets identify the same described objects across steps without manufacturing runtime REF identities. Spatial relations use the existing spatial-relation category; via is a finite ordered list of traversed areas, not extra stopping destinations.
- Members: describe_place(target: TERM, destination: TERM, relation: STRING) -> TERM describes placing that object in the stated spatial relation to its destination; describe_pick_up(target: TERM) -> TERM describes acquiring/holding the identified object; describe_walk(destination: TERM, via?: LIST[TERM]) -> TERM describes walking to the destination through supplied intermediate areas; describe_turn_left() -> TERM describes turning left relative to the instructed actor's current orientation without specifying an angle; describe_turn_around() -> TERM describes reversing facing orientation, not backward walking or a circular route.
- Exceptions: Omitted via specifies no route; left does not imply a quarter-turn angle; target descriptions neither create a runtime reference nor establish that the actor already holds the object. Additional selection/placement constraints may be supplied through UTTER.constraints. The family name is organizational, not callable vocabulary.
- Example: `TERM describe_walk(destination=t1.lexical_label_3, via=[subject_2]) -> describe_walk_3 : TERM`, then `UTTER propose(target=describe_walk_3)`.
- Proposed record: {"symbol":"describe_place","kind":"constructor","signature":"TERM describe_place(target: TERM, destination: TERM, relation: STRING) -> TERM","definition":"Describes placing the identified object in the stated spatial relation to the destination; relation must be a governed spatial-relation value. Does not execute, assert completion, or create a runtime reference.","not":"A completed placement EVENT or an executable place operation.","aliases":[]}
- Proposed record: {"symbol":"describe_pick_up","kind":"constructor","signature":"TERM describe_pick_up(target: TERM) -> TERM","definition":"Describes acquiring and holding the identified physical object. Does not execute, assert success, or create a runtime reference.","not":"Picking an option in a UI or reporting an observed acquisition.","aliases":[]}
- Proposed record: {"symbol":"describe_walk","kind":"constructor","signature":"TERM describe_walk(destination: TERM, via?: LIST[TERM]) -> TERM","definition":"Describes walking to the identified destination, through the ordered areas in via when supplied. Areas must be location descriptions; omission leaves the route unspecified and does not execute or assert travel.","not":"Web navigation or a list of required stops.","aliases":[]}
- Proposed record: {"symbol":"describe_turn_left","kind":"constructor","signature":"TERM describe_turn_left() -> TERM","definition":"Describes turning the instructed actor's body/view orientation left relative to its current facing; no exact angle is specified. Does not execute or assert a turn.","not":"Moving to the left side of another object.","aliases":[]}
- Proposed record: {"symbol":"describe_turn_around","kind":"constructor","signature":"TERM describe_turn_around() -> TERM","definition":"Describes reversing the instructed actor's facing orientation. Does not execute or assert the turn, and specifies no locomotion.","not":"Walking backward or moving around a landmark.","aliases":[]}

### S2 | type: add | dimension: member-family | symbol: room_spatial_relations
- Needs: n8/n9 (t2:s2).
- Searches tried: search "across from opposite facing", "at wall boundary"; widen "on wall at boundary across from couch"; closest other_side_of means the other side of a reference object, on means resting atop, wall is only a landmark, and spatial_constraint accepts a relation but does not define one.
- Shared category rules: STRING spatial-relation values for spatial_constraint and spatial_state; directional/frame dependencies remain explicit translation ambiguities when not supplied. These are reviewed relational meanings, not open-label stand-ins for propositions.
- Members: wall_position — located along the room-boundary wall identified by the reference, preserving colloquial "on the wall" furniture location without asserting support/mounting geometry; across_from — located opposite the reference across an intervening spatial area, not merely on the reference object's far side.
- Exceptions: wall_position requires a wall reference; neither value implies exact distance, touching, facing orientation of the object's own front, or a particular coordinate system. across_from does not require literal facing of object fronts.
- Example: `TERM spatial_constraint(object=lexical_label_2, reference=lexical_label_4, relation=wall_position) -> spatial_constraint_2 : TERM`.
- Contrast: A shelf resting on top of a cabinet uses on; an end table described as "on the wall" uses wall_position. A landmark on the couch's far side is other_side_of, whereas a table across the room from the couch is across_from.
- Proposed record: {"symbol":"wall_position","kind":"value","category":"spatial-relation","signature":"STRING","definition":"Located along the room-boundary wall identified by the reference, including colloquial furniture placement 'on the wall'; does not specify mounting, support, contact, exact distance or geometry. The reference must identify a wall.","not":"Resting atop a wall or necessarily mounted on its surface.","aliases":[]}
- Proposed record: {"symbol":"across_from","kind":"value","category":"spatial-relation","signature":"STRING","definition":"Located opposite the reference across an intervening area in the supplied spatial context. Does not imply exact distance or orientation of either object's front.","not":"Merely on the far side of the reference object, or adjacent to it.","aliases":[]}
